WHY THIS IS NOT AN OPEN-SOURCE LICENCE
--------------------------------------
This repository previously carried the MIT Licence. The Official Rules do not
require an entrant to license their own work under any particular terms --
every mention of "licence" in those Rules concerns either third-party software
the entrant *uses*, or the evaluation licence granted to Google. MIT was
adopted because an earlier draft of `docs/eligibility_statement.md` had
already asserted it, not because it was chosen deliberately. It was replaced
in Audit Wave 27 once that was noticed, because MIT actively invites
closed-source commercial reuse of this work, which is not the author's intent.

